# SHG Portal — Core Conventions

Self Help Group management portal. Keep changes simple, vertical-slice, and compilable after every batch.

## Stack (locked)

- Next.js 16 App Router, React 19, TypeScript strict
- MongoDB + Mongoose, Auth.js v5 (NextAuth), MUI v9, Zod, react-hook-form
- Read `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` before using Next.js APIs — this version has breaking changes

## Architecture

Feature-first layout under `src/features/{feature}/`:

| Layer | Path | Responsibility |
|-------|------|----------------|
| Domain | `domain/` | Pure types, constants, business rules — no DB or React |
| Services | `services/` | DB access, orchestration; export via `services/index.ts` |
| Internal | `services/internal/` | Private helpers — not exported from feature barrel |
| UI | `ui/` | MUI components — no business logic |
| Validation | `validation.ts` | Zod schemas shared by services and forms |

Models live in `src/models/`. Shared utilities in `src/lib/`. Use `@/` path alias.

## Principles

- **Simple over abstract** — no DTO layers, repository classes, or extra mapper interfaces
- **Functions over classes** — `create()`, `update()`, `list()`, `close()`, `activate()`
- **Throw `AppError`** from `@/lib/errors` for expected failures; API routes catch and return JSON
- **Mobile-first** MUI UI; currency/date formatting via `@/lib/utils`
- **Prettier**: double quotes, 100 print width, organize imports on save

## Domain modules

Financial Years → Meetings → Members → Loans → Reports → Auth/ACL

Each module has business rules (e.g. one active FY, closed FY is read-only). Check `docs/` and existing feature code before changing rules.
